"Explain Gandhi's Satyagraha and its idea. @ Satyagraha emphasised the power of truth and the need to search for truth, and was based on non-violence @ Gandhi believed that if the cause was true, physical force was not necessary and the oppressor could be persuaded to see the truth @ He applied it in Champaran in 1916-17 for the indigo peasants, in Kheda in 1917 for peasants hit by crop failure, and in Ahmedabad in 1918 for cotton mill workers @ It was non-violent, so people of all classes and communities could join @ This attracted masses to the Congress and made it a truly mass movement",
