"Explain Jallianwala Bagh. @ The incident took place in Amritsar on 13 April 1919, the day of the Baisakhi festival @ A large crowd had gathered in the enclosed ground of Jallianwala Bagh, some to protest against the government's measures @ General Dyer entered, blocked the exit points and ordered firing without warning @ Hundreds of unarmed people, including women and children, were killed @ Outrage followed and it hardened Indian opposition to British rule, and martial law was imposed in Punjab",
