"Explain Civil Disobedience Movement. @ The causes were the Simon Commission, Irwin's vague offer of dominion status and the Lahore Congress demand for Purna Swaraj @ Gandhi began the Salt March in March 1930 and broke the salt law at Dandi @ People boycotted foreign cloth, picketed liquor shops and refused to pay taxes @ Peasants, women, business groups and workers took part in large numbers @ It ended with the Gandhi-Irwin Pact in March 1931, and was resumed later but lost momentum by 1934",
